/*
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Launchpad Nextflow config for DRAGEN on AWS Batch F2 instances
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Paste into the "Nextflow config" field of the Launchpad pipeline (or the
    launch form). The compute environment must be a Seqera Batch Forge one with
    DRAGEN enabled (marketplace or BYOL AMI), an F2 DRAGEN instance type,
    Fusion v2, Wave and fast instance storage (NVMe).

    Why the Launchpad and not the compute environment's Nextflow config:
    for DRAGEN-enabled compute environments, Seqera Platform appends its own
    aws.batch.volumes line (without libdragen or /ephemeral) AFTER the compute
    environment's Nextflow config. aws.batch.volumes is a single value, so that
    line silently replaces one set in the compute environment. The Launchpad
    config is applied last, so a value set here wins.

    These settings depend on the compute environment, not the pipeline:
      - the libdragen.so version must match the DRAGEN version of the AMI
      - /scratch/fusion:/tmp needs Fusion; /ephemeral needs NVMe storage

    Without the /ephemeral scratch, DRAGEN writing straight to the Fusion work
    directory fails with "async_io.cpp ... I/O Error err=5" (exit 134).

    Retries: on DRAGEN hosts, Platform's boot script restarts the ECS agent about
    a minute after the host boots. A DRAGEN task running at that moment is killed
    (exit 143); one starting then never starts ("Unable to get execution role
    credentials for task", exit status Integer.MAX_VALUE). The DRAGEN retry rule
    below is the pipeline default (conf/base.config) plus Integer.MAX_VALUE, so
    both are retried on the same host; real DRAGEN errors still stop the run.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/

aws.batch.volumes = '/scratch/fusion:/tmp,/opt/edico,/var/lib/edico,/lib64/libdragen.so.4.4.4,/ephemeral'

process {
    withName: '.*:DRAGEN' {
        scratch          = '/ephemeral'
        containerOptions = '-e FUSION_CACHE_LOCATION=/ephemeral -e FUSION_COMPACT_SYMLINKS=true -e FUSION_STOP_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT=2h'
    }
    withLabel: 'dragen' {
        errorStrategy = { task.exitStatus in ((130..145) + 104 + Integer.MAX_VALUE) ? 'retry' : 'finish' }
        maxRetries    = 3
    }
}
